{"name":"Freshwater Marsh","hex":"#535644","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"freshwater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Living in fresh water.","Consisting of fresh water."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of fresh water.","Alternative form of fresh water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freshwater"},{"term":"marsh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of low, wet land, often with tall grass or herbaceous plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Freshwater marsh","blocks":[{"text":"A freshwater marsh is a non-forested marsh wetland that contains shallow fresh water, and is continuously or frequently flooded. Freshwater marshes primarily consist of sedges, grasses, and emergent plants. Freshwater marshes are usually found near the mouths of rivers, along lakes, or are present in low lying areas with low drainage like abandoned oxbow lakes. Unlike its counterpart the salt marsh, which is regularly flushed with sea water, freshwater marshes receive the majority of their water from surface water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Naselle_River_seen_from_US_101.JPG/330px-Naselle_River_seen_from_US_101.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freshwater_marsh","wikidata":"Q31455"},{"title":"Fresh water","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh water or freshwater is any naturally occurring liquid or frozen water containing low concentrations of dissolved salts and other total dissolved solids. The term excludes seawater and brackish water, but it does include non-salty mineral-rich waters, such as chalybeate springs. Fresh water may encompass frozen and meltwater in ice sheets, ice caps, glaciers, snowfields and icebergs, natural precipitations such as rainfall, snowfall, hail/sleet and graupel, and surface runoffs that form inland bodies of water such as wetlands, ponds, lakes, rivers, streams, as well as groundwater contained in aquifers, subterranean rivers and lakes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Amazonas%2C_Iquitos_-_Leticia%2C_Kolumbien_%2811472506936%29.jpg/330px-Amazonas%2C_Iquitos_-_Leticia%2C_Kolumbien_%2811472506936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_water","wikidata":"Q102192"},{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Early_Spring_Marsh.jpg/500px-Early_Spring_Marsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Early_Spring_Marsh.jpg/500px-Early_Spring_Marsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Freshwater marsh in Kittery Point, Maine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarly_Spring_Marsh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Creek_%28fen%29_in_Pennsylvania.jpg/500px-Creek_%28fen%29_in_Pennsylvania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Creek_%28fen%29_in_Pennsylvania.jpg/1280px-Creek_%28fen%29_in_Pennsylvania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.